{"kind":"report","text":"Checker review of the evidence-rules slice at head 110da571846d03d0a5daa134e28ea67532b045ec, tree 48460dab21a245052e5d27673ea8e34213e6d0b2, for request a53e1464 and review request f9f6b80d. Verdict: APPROVED.\n\nThe head adds six commits to 9c15879a, which I reviewed in 8b1165f8. I read the implementation note at this head first. Then I read the code diff from 9c15879a to the repaired code head 00834f19, the witness changes, the evidence receipts and the documents.\n\n## Against review 8b1165f8\n\n1. A second checker key stranded a room job. Resolved.\n   - The lane `check` and `check-error` acts now record a result and change nothing on the job. Witnesses N4 and N8 assert that the act's entry has no state effect and no `decidedBy` effect on the job.\n   - Destination checks the delivery in a new type rule, `evidence-result-source-v17`, before it selects a bound holder. The rule reads the admitted record and confirms the sender's entry. For a room job, it passes the frozen marked key to `readEvidenceDecisionV17`, which refuses any other actor. A wrong key therefore spends neither the funded result operation nor the held duty.\n   - Only a `check-decision` with status `decided` and reason `counted` settles the job. Its guard `not-this-counted-result` binds the exact result fact, job, binding digest and tree. The outcome comes from the opened result.\n   - N4 sends two claims signed with Vic's key, a second key of the same member. The job, the Native record and the held duty stay equal to their earlier values. Paul's marked key then counts on the same job. N8 refuses an unmarked `check-error` on an audit job, and the marked pass counts after it.\n   - The control `repair-native-key-guard-control-1` removes `resultKey` from the Destination call. N4 then fails by assertion: the delivery applies instead of refusing. The control restores the source.\n   - Member-source jobs keep their current key eligibility, as the request states.\n2. The implementation note's writing. Resolved.\n   - The note uses plain names, such as \"Register 22\" and \"Node 78\", in place of abbreviations.\n   - It has no literal Rests-On lines. Each governing act appears with its full identifier.\n   - Prose lines fit in 79 characters. Only full identifiers and table rows are longer.\n   - The base line names Main 06e4d33f as the start and Main 8659af46 as the merge.\n3. The design note's status rows. Resolved. The rows for sources, reuse, the work and landing stages, and the published stage with holds now say what the first slice builds.\n4. \"User authorized deployments\". Resolved. The note no longer has the statement. \"Remaining acceptance\" says that the planner owns rollout.\n\nThe recut also takes three points that did not block. The request and the primary artifact rest on live bases: a891555c, a53e1464 and c20152ef. `docs/security/entry-points.md` now lists the internal methods `jobState`, `workSourceState` and `stageSnapshot`. It also states the source reads before the key check and the 15-minute replay window.\n\n## Checks at this head\n\n- The worktree is clean at 110da571. A merge onto main 8659af46 gives the head tree 48460dab.\n- From 00834f19 to the head, only the implementation note and the manifest change. Ruling 31962e1f permits that tail.\n- Gate 4 passes at 00834f19, tree c3d6e7a5: exit 0, 935.8 seconds, clean status after the run. Node 78, Counting 55, plain 3,092 with one skip, Native 836 with two skips.\n- `repair-native-protocol-1` passes 10 of 10 tests in the two Native files at 00834f19.\n- The manifest has SHA-256 4a60138a, as the request states. It follows ruling 4e199bd8:\n  - all 1,386 listed files match by size and SHA-256;\n  - `prior` matches its digest 4eec5e38, and its SHA256SUMS reruns clean over 27,219 files;\n  - `finalization` matches its digest 83483511, and its SHA256SUMS reruns clean over 14 files;\n  - the root SHA256SUMS has SHA-256 982eb3be and covers all 29,533 other files, with none unlisted and none writable.\n- The `prior` SHA256SUMS equals the original collection's root SHA256SUMS. `prior-manifest.json` equals the original manifest f3e3c6cf. So the original sealed collection is unchanged.\n- The Destination 17 pin moves to 96390fe5 in `native-declarations.generated.ts` and `versions.test.ts`. The lane digests in `digests4.ts`, `evidence-lane-pins.generated.ts` and `docs/lanes-reference.md` agree. `repair-final-document-reproduction-1` regenerates the views and the page assets at ede0777f with no difference.\n- The recut changes no file under the kernel or `packages/derive`.\n- check-doc-links on an export of the head: 736 links, 0 broken.\n- check-commit-messages from 8659af46: 90 checked, 0 flagged.\n- check-notes from 8659af46: one warning, for the manifest size.\n- `git diff --check`: clean.\n\n## Points that do not block\n\n1. Results on a decided job. The lane `check` guard still admits results on a job in `passed`, `failed` or `errored`, and `result` allows 512 items. Any key of the checker member can add results that Destination then refuses. They use up the lane's result limit. The member is trusted, so this is not a hole, but a later version can refuse results on a final job.\n2. A frozen job reads `requested`. After a rotation, Destination decides the old job's result as `wrong-source`. The lane job stays `requested` until TIME, with the decision in `nativeDecision`. A view of the lane should show the Native reason.\n3. The manifest is 202,723 bytes, over the 40,960-byte limit in check-notes. It was 4.7 MB.\n4. Small writing points:\n   - the receipt table headings \"Check / command record\" and \"Exit/timeout\" use slashes;\n   - `docs/architecture.md` says \"member/key pair\";\n   - the line in `docs/architecture.md` that starts \"Reuse uses a bounded index\" is over 79 characters.\n\n## Architecture\n\nThe repair puts settlement in one place. The lane records a claim, and Destination decides whether it counts. That matches the design note: Destination judges source and authority. The new rule reuses the existing decision reader with one optional field, `resultKey`. The repair adds no kernel operation, wire field, slot or wider bound. Approved.\n\n## Security\n\n- A room job counts only a result signed by the frozen marked key. The check runs before Destination draws the funded operation or the held duty, so a second key of the same member cannot spend either.\n- Destination checks current authority again when it counts.\n- The lane settles only on an authenticated `check-decision` from the job's Destination. That decision names the exact result, binding and tree.\n- The control shows that N4 detects removal of the key check.\n- Member-source behavior is unchanged and documented.\n\nApproved.\n\n## Simplification\n\nThe repair removes the lane's own settlement effects and the decision reader's state check, and moves both into one counted notice. It adds one type rule and one optional field. That is less machinery than the head it replaces. Approved.\n\n## Conclusions\n\n- Architecture: approved.\n- Security: approved.\n- Simplification: approved.\n- The request's checks: the source authorization and the job lifecycle hold in the code and in N4 and N8. The note citations and the directory indices verify under ruling 4e199bd8.\n\nThe landing check will follow the landing.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:7037018ec929d89dfb62363ec51f556ac04d46fa","binding":"assigned","head":"110da571846d03d0a5daa134e28ea67532b045ec","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:16516d164e843448123edf849be07c2e568ed743\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:a891555c470d4693e466b9c5240b5ed35a95b388\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:16516d164e843448123edf849be07c2e568ed743","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}